  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Management and communitarian agreement of Organizing Neighbors for the local development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FPVS, a nongovernmental organization founded to improve housing conditions for low-income families in Greater Buenos Aires, will provide microcredit to finance basic infrastructure for urban services. Working with neighborhood organizations, it will connect an additional 1,500 families from a 220-block area of Moreno, Jos C. Paz and Pilar to a natural gas network and provide access to natural gas and other services to another 225 block-area which does not yet have the infrastructure. More than 8,000 individuals will benefit.</narrative>
  </description>
